# Cloudinary setup
# 1. Create a free Cloudinary account.
# 2. Copy the cloud name + API key from the dashboard.
# 3. Keep the API secret private; it is only used by server-side routes.
# 4. Set this as a Netlify environment variable for deployed builds too.
#    The public cloud name used by the client is derived from this URL in next.config.ts.
CLOUDINARY_URL=cloudinary://API_KEY:API_SECRET@CLOUD_NAME

# Turso setup — durable SQLite-compatible DB for the scrapbook note board
# (notes, cover, and memories are stored as one JSON row in the note_board table
# of the birthday-notes-endcall database).
# 1. Create the database in the Turso dashboard.
# 2. Copy the database URL (libsql://...) and create an auth token there.
# 3. Set both as Netlify environment variables for deployed builds.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=